{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to present an Ed25519 host certificate signed by a locally generated SSH CA. A strict client trusting only that CA connected successfully without a pinned host key. Configuration persisted across the mandatory node restart.","actions_performed":["Generated a protected Ed25519 SSH host CA on node1.","Signed the existing Ed25519 host key for principals node1 and 10.100.100.10.","Configured sshd with HostCertificate and validated/reloaded the service.","Verified successful CA-only SSH connections before and after reboot.","Safely restarted node1 and confirmed its boot identity changed.","Removed the temporary client authentication material used for testing."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SSH CA and signed host certificate configured","command_ids":["cmd-2a85778f01114db1","cmd-cf75fe6c02e74fc0"],"summary":"Shows the effective HostCertificate configuration, matching signing CA, certificate principals, secure CA private-key permissions, and active sshd."},{"requirement":"Client connects by trusting the CA without pinning the host key","command_ids":["cmd-0a56d51809034307","cmd-b0b7fcf71b4d4e8e"],"summary":"Both tests used one @cert-authority entry and zero pinned host-key entries. OpenSSH matched the ED25519 host certificate to the CA and authenticated successfully."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-1a9d501b01fd4b66","cmd-276e23eb361f4d95","cmd-bd0dc2f0e8894d62","cmd-b0b7fcf71b4d4e8e"],"summary":"Captures the healthy pre-restart baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, fully running system, recovered sshd listener/configuration, and successful post-restart CA-only connection."}]}
